\ A raise inside a `choose` predicate. The compiled `choose` intrinsic inlines the predicate
\ invocation, so the chain carries a `choose` row at the call site but not the prelude-internal
\ `call` row an interpreted run shows. The interpreted twin is error_frames_choose.1z, which
\ keeps the same line layout and pins the interpreted shape.

pick-bigger: ( a b -- x ) [ [ + 0 > ] choose 0 + ] ;

1 "x" pick-bigger .
